Sanskrit]"],"verses":[{"text":["namas te narasiṁhāya","    prahlādāhlāda-dāyine","hiraṇyakaśipor vakṣaḥ-","    śilā-ṭaṅka-nakhālaye"],"translation":["I offer my obeisances to Lord Nṛsiṁha, who gives joy to Prahlād Mahārāj and whose nails are like chisels on the stonelike chest of the demon Hiraṇyakaśipu."],"isLong":false},{"text":["ito nṛsiṁhaḥ parato nṛsiṁho","    yato yato yāmi tato nṛsiṁhaḥ","bahir nṛsiṁho hṛdaye nṛsiṁho","    nṛsiṁham ādiṁ śaraṇaṁ prapadye"],"translation":["Lord Nṛsiṁha is here and also there. Wherever I go Lord Nṛsiṁha is there. He is in the heart and is outside as well. I surrender to Lord Nṛsiṁha, the origin of all things and the supreme refuge.\\","*(Śrīla Vyasādeva)*"],"isLong":false},{"text":["tava kara-kamala-vare nakham adbhuta-śṛṅgaṁ","dalita-hiraṇyakaśipu-tanu-bhṛṅgam","keśava dhṛta-narahari-rūpa jaya jagadīśa hare"],"translation":["O Keśava! O Lord of the universe! O Lord Hari, who have assumed the form of half-man, half-lion! All glories to You! Just as one can easily crush a wasp between one’s fingernails, so in the same way the body of the wasplike demon Hiraṇyakaśipu has been ripped apart by the wonderful pointed nails on Your beautiful lotus hands.\\","*(Śrīla Jayadev Goswāmī)*"],"isLong":false}],"resources":{"audio":[{"title":"Manasa Krishna Prabhu","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/huron/namas-te-narasimhaya","personSlug":"manasa-krishna-prabhu"}]},"hasWbw":false,"hasVersesText":true,"hasVersesTranslations":true,"hasLongVerses":false,"fullInlineWbw":false},"telegraphUrl":"https://telegra.ph/Śrī-Nṛsiṁha-Praṇām-02-22"},"head":{"canonical":"/en/namas-te-narasimhaya/","description":"Śrī Nṛsiṁha Praṇām — a Vaiṣṇava song by Śrīla Vyasādeva with lyrics, English translation and word-by-word meaning. From Kirtan Guide.","title":"Śrī Nṛsiṁha Praṇām. [Sanskrit] | Kirtan Site"},"kind":"song","route":{"kind":"item","bookId":"en","slug":"namas-te-narasimhaya"}}